{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "2: Session detail & token trend",
  "description": "End-to-end: one click on a session, through the local-only detail query, to the inline SVG token-trend graph. Every step embeds the numbered sequence diagram and points at the exact code for that step.",
  "nextTour": "3: Live updates",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — Click a session",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/renderer/src/views/sessions/SessionsView.tsx",
      "line": 380,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-10.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 1 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `Dev → SessionDetail: Click a session`**\n\nClicking a row's `onSelect` sets the selection, and the right-hand pane mounts a `SessionDetail` keyed by source and session id — so a new selection always starts a fresh load."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — Ask the data host for the document",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/renderer/src/views/sessions/SessionDetail.tsx",
      "line": 91,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-11.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 2 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `SessionDetail → DetailRenderer: sessions.detail`**\n\n`SessionDetail` calls `dataHost.call('sessions.detail', source, sessionId, theme)`. In the data host that lands on `DetailRenderer.renderDocument`; the renderer process itself stores nothing."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — Ask the source for detail",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/detail/detailRenderer.ts",
      "line": 287,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-12.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 3 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `DetailRenderer → TelemetryService: getSessionDetail(key)`**\n\n`DetailRenderer` looks the owning source up in core's `SourceRegistry` and asks it for `getSessionDetail(sessionId)`. The Copilot source forwards straight to `TelemetryService`. Parses are memoized by index stamp, so reopening a session is cheap."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Service delegates to the DB",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/telemetry/telemetryService.ts",
      "line": 721,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-13.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 4 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `TelemetryService → TelemetryDatabase: getSessionDetail()`**\n\n`TelemetryService.getSessionDetail` delegates to the database layer. The desktop injects a native backend whose short-lived read transaction pins a consistent view of the archive without copying it; the source database is never written."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5 — Local-only detail assembly",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/telemetry/database.ts",
      "line": 879,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-14.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 5 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `TelemetryDatabase → TelemetryService: SessionDetail (turns, tokens)`**\n\n`TelemetryDatabase.getSessionDetail` assembles prompts, responses, turns, and agent-tree totals for local display. The tree traversal and numeric write deltas are reused across rollups within the immutable read view; raw tool arguments are discarded. Raw detail stays in-process and is only ever rendered on this machine."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 6 — Render the document",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/detail/detailRenderer.ts",
      "line": 117,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-15.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 6 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `DetailRenderer → sessionDetailHtml: renderSessionDetailHtml()`**\n\n`renderDocument` calls core's `renderSessionDetailHtml(detail, deviations, ...)`, building the whole document — styles, tabs, and a per-render nonce for the content security policy."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 7 — Call renderTokenTrend",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/views/sessionDetailHtml.ts",
      "line": 1070,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-16.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 7 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `sessionDetailHtml → sessionDetailHtml: renderTokenTrend(modelTurns)`**\n\nThe content's tree-summary card calls `renderTokenTrend(modelTurns, trendSessions)` to draw the per-turn token trend graph. Charts stay eager; event rows in large timelines are deferred until their disclosure opens."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 8 — Build the inline SVG",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/views/sessionDetailHtml.ts",
      "line": 1307,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-17.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 8 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `sessionDetailHtml → DetailRenderer: HTML + SVG trend graph`**\n\n`renderTokenTrend` buckets model turns into inline SVG with an empty state for fewer than two points. The nonce-authorized controller handles legend filtering and lazy event pagination without an external chart library."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 9 — Mount or live-update the frame",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/renderer/src/views/sessions/SessionDetail.tsx",
      "line": 332,
      "description": "![2: Session detail & token trend](.tours/diagrams/d-18.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 9 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `DetailRenderer → Dev: document in a sandboxed iframe`**\n\nThe document is stashed behind a URL and loaded into an iframe sandboxed to `allow-scripts` only, so it cannot touch the app's DOM, storage or preload bridge. Later refreshes post a `{ type: 'update' }` message that swaps the body while preserving open sections, the active tab, and scroll."
    }
  ]
}
